      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The answer is straightforward: according to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key completely out of its own process environment by using a **local secrets loader** that:\n\n1. **Reads the key at startup** from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file\n2. **Injects it only into child processes** \u2014 specifically, into the environment of the spawned Ingest (and Query) agent processes, immediately before they start\n3. **Never mutates the Hub\u0027s own process environment** \u2014 the key is never written into the Hub\u0027s own variables\n\nThis design ensures that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, the attacker cannot leak the credential simply by inspecting the Hub\u0027s environment variables \u2014 the key only exists inside the short-lived child processes that actually need it to call the Anthropic API.",
